export anchor HeartMonitorStyle:
    number: 385
    screen: FitnessTracker
    name: Heart monitor
    idea: The day shown on a bedside style monitor, with stacked signal channels on a fine grid, a live trace for heart rate, the week drawn as a rhythm strip of beats, and the five zone colours leading every reading.
    base: dark
    palette:
        bg: #040706, the case around the screen
        screen: #07100d, every channel, the side panel and the style sheet
        grid: #11231c, the fine 8px grid behind signals
        gridMaj: #1a3a2e, the 40px grid and the rhythm baseline
        line: #244236, channel dividers and field borders
        ink: #e6f2ec, text, readings and goal ticks
        muted: #9db8ac, labels, units and rest days
        trace: #43f59b, the heart trace, ring progress, rhythm strip, plan pip and primary button
        z1: #78b6ff, zone 1 Easy and deep sleep
        z2: #43e0a0, zone 2 Aerobic
        z3: #ffd23f, zone 3 Tempo and the average heart rate
        z4: #ff9c45, zone 4 Threshold
        z5: #ff6b7a, zone 5 Max
        onZ: #04120b, text on zone and trace fills
    type:
        Readings use Segoe UI, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial at weight 300
        with tabular numbers, 52px for heart rate, 44px for side parameters
        and 40px for ring values. Channel labels and meta use ui-monospace,
        SF Mono, Cascadia Mono, Menlo, Consolas at 12px, caps at 700 tracked
        0.08em. Body is 14px at 1.45.
    layout:
        One monitor case 1260px wide with an 18px radius and an inset black
        bezel. A status strip across the top holds Brightwork Move, Today
        with the date, a green heartbeat glyph with Last session 42 min 16
        s, and Today, Week and Plan as small mono tabs. Below, a main column
        of channels beside a 300px side panel. Every channel is a row of
        three cells, a 96px mono label cell, a signal cell on a fine green
        grid and a 190px reading cell. The HR channel draws a repeating
        heartbeat trace and reads 152 bpm in zone 3 yellow with a Z3 tag.
        The Zones channel spans the signal and reading cells with one strip
        split into five zone colours, each with its own stripe pattern and Z
        label, and a key of Z number, name and minutes. Move, Exercise and
        Stand channels show a glowing green fill with a ring dot at the
        percent, a dotted remainder, a white goal tick with the percent, and
        a reading of value over goal with open and the amount to go. The
        bottom of the column is the week as a rhythm strip, one beat per day
        with height by distance and the figure above, flat line and rest for
        empty days, day names under it and today marked with a diamond,
        headed with 23.7 km, 4 runs and 3 rest. The side panel stacks the
        Evening run with a Done tag and four parameters, Sleep 7 h 12 min
        with a two part bar for deep sleep, and a green outlined next
        session box with twelve plan pips, Long run 14 km and View plan.
        Below 1000px the side panel moves under the channels in two columns.
        At 375px label and reading share a row above the signal, and the
        rhythm strip scrolls inside its own area.
    spacing: An 8px unit and an 8px signal grid. Channels sit edge to edge with 1px dividers and 12 to 16px inner padding.
    density: High. Every reading is a channel row, all visible at once like a monitor.
    corners: 18px on the monitor case, 8px on the next session box, 3 to 6px on tags and controls.
    borders: 1px dark green dividers between every channel and column.
    shadows: An inset black bezel around the screen and a soft green glow on progress fills.
    icons:
        A heartbeat glyph for the run. Zones carry a Z number, a name and a
        distinct stripe pattern. Rings say open with a hollow circle. Rest
        days are a flat line with the word rest. The average heart rate tag
        has a triangle.
    focus: A 2px white outline offset 2px with a 5px green halo.
    tone: Clinical short labels such as HR, Zones, avg, open, to go and Week rhythm.
